1
00:00:54,530 --> 00:00:57,530
Hi, big guy.

2
00:00:57,530 --> 00:00:59,530
That must be Rita Mae.

3
00:00:59,530 --> 00:01:01,530
She sure got here quickly.

4
00:01:01,530 --> 00:01:02,530
That's a good sign.

5
00:01:02,530 --> 00:01:04,530
She must like you and your work, Marilyn.

6
00:01:04,530 --> 00:01:06,530
I think she's just anxious to see Max.

7
00:01:06,530 --> 00:01:16,530
She loves children.

8
00:01:16,530 --> 00:01:18,530
Hi, Marilyn.

9
00:01:18,530 --> 00:01:21,530
Welcome.

10
00:01:21,530 --> 00:01:23,530
It's so nice of you to come.

11
00:01:23,530 --> 00:01:26,530
Oh, I just wanted to see your baby, Max.

12
00:01:26,530 --> 00:01:28,530
Hello, Rita Mae.

13
00:01:28,530 --> 00:01:30,530
I haven't seen you since the hospital.

14
00:01:30,530 --> 00:01:33,530
I'm Ellen Stewart, Marilyn's mother-in-law.

15
00:01:33,530 --> 00:01:34,530
We met at the hospital.

16
00:01:34,530 --> 00:01:35,530
How are you?

17
00:01:35,530 --> 00:01:36,530
How are you?

18
00:01:36,530 --> 00:01:39,530
Oh, and there is Max!

19
00:01:39,530 --> 00:01:43,530
Oh! My, how he's grown!

20
00:01:43,530 --> 00:01:47,530
A little present for Max.

21
00:01:47,530 --> 00:01:51,530
Oh, it's beautiful, Rita Mae!

22
00:01:51,530 --> 00:01:52,530
You shouldn't have.

23
00:01:52,530 --> 00:01:53,530
It's nothing.

24
00:01:53,530 --> 00:01:54,530
It's just a little present for Max.

25
00:01:54,530 --> 00:01:58,530
Can I get you some coffee or tea or a cold drink, Rita Mae?

26
00:01:58,530 --> 00:01:59,530
Oh, nothing, thank you.

27
00:01:59,530 --> 00:02:03,530
Well, I will leave you two to talk.

28
00:02:03,530 --> 00:02:05,530
Come on, you big guy.

29
00:02:05,530 --> 00:02:06,530
Yes, come on.

30
00:02:06,530 --> 00:02:08,530
That's it.

31
00:02:08,530 --> 00:02:09,530
It's nice seeing you.

32
00:02:09,530 --> 00:02:11,530
Let me know if you need anything.

33
00:02:11,530 --> 00:02:12,530
Thanks, Ellen.

34
00:02:12,530 --> 00:02:13,530
Thanks, Ellen.

35
00:02:13,530 --> 00:02:18,530
OK, Marilyn.

36
00:02:18,530 --> 00:02:20,530
You sounded like you've made a decision

37
00:02:20,530 --> 00:02:21,530
when you called me.

38
00:02:21,530 --> 00:02:24,530
I have made a decision, Rita Mae.

39
00:02:24,530 --> 00:02:26,530
I've decided to stay at home and be a full-time mother.

40
00:02:26,530 --> 00:02:30,530
I'm disappointed, but I respect your decision.

41
00:02:30,530 --> 00:02:33,530
If I had a child as cute as Max,

42
00:02:33,530 --> 00:02:34,530
I might do the same thing.

43
00:02:34,530 --> 00:02:36,530
But I haven't finished telling you

44
00:02:36,530 --> 00:02:37,530
the other half of my decision.

45
00:02:37,530 --> 00:02:38,530
The other half?

46
00:02:38,530 --> 00:02:39,530
Yes.

47
00:02:39,530 --> 00:02:41,530
I think I can stay at home

48
00:02:41,530 --> 00:02:44,530
and take care of Max and continue my career.

49
00:02:44,530 --> 00:02:47,530
Sounds interesting.

50
00:02:47,530 --> 00:02:49,530
Let me hear it.

51
00:02:49,530 --> 00:02:50,530
Do you remember

52
00:02:50,530 --> 00:02:52,530
our talks about custom-designed dresses for the boutique?

53
00:02:52,530 --> 00:02:53,530
I sure do.

54
00:02:53,530 --> 00:02:58,530
Why can't I design dresses for you here at home?

55
00:02:58,530 --> 00:02:59,930
And make them here.

56
00:02:59,930 --> 00:03:01,830
Have the fittings here, too.

57
00:03:01,830 --> 00:03:04,930
And I could do the selling and the pricing at the boutique.

58
00:03:04,930 --> 00:03:05,530
Exactly.

59
00:03:05,530 --> 00:03:07,530
Oh!

60
00:03:07,530 --> 00:03:09,530
What kind of dresses would you design?

61
00:03:09,530 --> 00:03:13,530
I've thought about that for some time.

62
00:03:13,530 --> 00:03:15,530
Yes?

63
00:03:15,530 --> 00:03:17,530
Wedding dresses.

64
00:03:17,530 --> 00:03:18,530
Wedding dresses?

65
00:03:18,530 --> 00:03:21,530
Brilliant idea!

66
00:03:21,530 --> 00:03:24,530
There's a big market today in wedding dresses.

67
00:03:24,530 --> 00:03:25,530
That's what I thought.

68
00:03:25,530 --> 00:03:26,530
I like the idea very much.

69
00:03:26,530 --> 00:03:28,530
And if it's successful,

70
00:03:28,530 --> 00:03:30,530
we can expand to all kinds of dresses.

71
00:03:30,530 --> 00:03:32,530
That's what I thought.

72
00:03:32,530 --> 00:03:34,530
As a matter of fact,

73
00:03:34,530 --> 00:03:37,530
I have a customer for your first wedding dress.

74
00:03:37,530 --> 00:03:39,530
My niece is getting married,

75
00:03:39,530 --> 00:03:42,530
and I've been trying to find just the right thing for her.

76
00:03:42,530 --> 00:03:45,530
Marilyn, you're going to design my niece's dress. Marilyn

77
00:03:45,530 --> 00:03:47,530
That'll be our first one,

78
00:03:47,530 --> 00:03:49,530
and then we'll use it to sell others.

79
00:03:49,530 --> 00:03:51,530
Do you really mean it?

80
00:03:51,530 --> 00:03:52,530
I really mean it.

81
00:03:52,530 --> 00:03:54,530
It's a simple idea, and it will work.

82
00:03:54,530 --> 00:03:57,530
You can certainly design dresses.

83
00:03:57,530 --> 00:03:58,530
I know that.

84
00:03:58,530 --> 00:04:01,530
And there's no reason why you can't do it from your home.

85
00:04:01,530 --> 00:04:03,530
I'm so excited!

86
00:04:03,530 --> 00:04:04,530
I can't wait to tell Richard!

87
00:04:04,530 --> 00:04:07,530
If I had a baby like Max,

88
00:04:07,530 --> 00:04:10,530
I'd want to stay home and be near him all the time, too.

89
00:04:10,530 --> 00:04:13,530
You're making the right decision

90
00:04:13,530 --> 00:04:15,530
for Max and for yourself too, Marilyn.

91
00:04:15,530 --> 00:04:17,530
It all sounds so easy.

92
00:04:17,530 --> 00:04:19,530
Now the hard work begins.

93
00:04:19,530 --> 00:04:20,530
Would you like

94
00:04:20,530 --> 00:04:23,530
to see some of my designs that I've been working on?

95
00:04:23,530 --> 00:04:24,530
I'd love to.

96
00:04:24,530 --> 00:04:30,530
Ooh! Oh, that's wonderful!

97
00:04:30,530 --> 00:04:33,530
Ooh ...
